item.description:
A grandfather who once feared the neonatal intensive care unit now calls it the place he belongs. Determined to challenge expectations of motherhood, ultrarunner Stephanie Case accomplished what no woman has before in Antarctica. A 15-year-old in Louisiana became the first child in the state to receive a groundbreaking gene therapy for sickle cell disease. A husband and wife in Birmingham, Alabama opened a grocery store in their neighborhood where residents had gone decades without one. Plus, more than 70 years after setting a transatlantic speed record, the SS United States made history again. &nbsp;

Host/Producer: Krista Bo Polanco&nbsp;

Producer: Eryn Mathewson, Ifeoma Dike&nbsp;

Showrunner: Felicia Patinkin&nbsp;

Editorial Support:&nbsp;Zach Goldbaum&nbsp;
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices

